      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "https://hello.vrchat.com/community-guidelines see the Groups Instances section.\n\n> \"Having an appeal process for your Group is ideal. However, you aren't *required* to have an appeal process for your Group. You are welcome to deny appeals, or inform users that “no appeals are accepted.”\"\n\nGroups are not required to have an appeal process.\n\n> \"Groups may moderate their instances how they see fit.\"\n\nThey own the instances, they can control who is or isn't allowed there. The moderation action is not automatically hateful, and VRChat won't care either way since it is only an issue between you and the group.\n\nYou should just find another instance or make your own instance.",
